# The gate of Krezk (docs/regions/krezk.md §4.1, docs/voice/krezk_guard.md, docs/voice/dmitri_krezkov.md).
# start: the watchman outside the shut gate speaks first (approach). The gate opens only for a reason; every reason
# ends in `opened`. Dmitri comes down to the gate himself when one is given. guard: the watchman afterwards.

~ start
if flag.krezk_gate_open
-> guard
endif
if flag.krezk_arrived
if flag.krezk_threatened
Krezk Watchman: Back again. My friend on the wall has kept an arrow out for you. He's sentimental that way. Found a reason yet, or just a louder voice?
else
Krezk Watchman: Back again. The gate's the same as you left it. Shut. Have you found a reason yet, or just more road?
endif
-> reasons
endif
set krezk_arrived
Narrator: The road ends at a wall of fitted grey stone three men high, older than the trees around it, with one gate of iron-banded black oak. A watchman stands before it with a spear and the look of a man paid to say one word.
Krezk Watchman: That's far enough. This is Krezk. The road stops here, and so do you.
if night
Krezk Watchman: And it's dark, which means I'd not open that gate for my own mother. She knows. She sleeps inside early.
endif
if guest:ireena and flag.ireena_destination == "krezk"
interject guest:ireena: Krezk. All that road, and it's a wall with a man in front of it.
endif
Krezk Watchman: We don't take strangers. Not for coin, not for pity, not for stories. The burgomaster opens that gate when there's a reason, and he decides what a reason is.
-> reasons

~ reasons
* We're travellers. We need shelter for the night. -> shelter
* [if guest:ireena] This is Ireena Kolyana, daughter of the burgomaster of Barovia. She needs refuge. -> ireena
* [if flag.abbot_vouched] The Abbot of St. Markovia sent us. He vouches for us. -> abbot
* [if flag.wizard_of_wines_hook or flag.wine_shortage_heard] Your wine comes from the Wizard of Wines, doesn't it? We know why it stopped. -> wine
* [if flag.krezk_wolves_driven_off] We just cleared the wolves off your doorstep. -> wolves
* [Cleric] I'm a priest. If you're this frightened of strangers, someone in there needs one. -> cleric
* [if not flag.krezk_persuade_tried and not flag.krezk_threatened] [Persuasion DC 14] Everyone in this valley needs someone to open a door. Be the one who does. -> persuade_ok | persuade_fail
* [Intimidation DC 16] Open it, or we'll find out how good your wall really is. -> cow_ok | cow_fail
* Is there anywhere up here that does take strangers? -> abbey_hint
* We'll come back. -> END

~ shelter
Krezk Watchman: Shelter's for Krezk. You're not Krezk. There's a ledge under the pines a mile back that keeps the snow off, if you don't mind the wolves minding you.
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Oh, we don't mind wolves, sir. Thank you kindly.
else
interject tag:blunt: He means it kindly. I think.
endif
-> reasons

~ abbey_hint
set krezk_abbey_directed
quest the_gate_of_krezk refused
Krezk Watchman: Up the mountain. The Abbey of St. Markovia. The track leaves the road just there, by the cairn, and climbs till your knees complain.
Krezk Watchman: The Abbot takes in anyone. That's the trouble with him. But the burgomaster listens to what he says about people, much as he hates to.
Narrator: He says "the Abbot" the way people say the name of a river that has drowned someone they knew.
-> END

~ persuade_ok
set krezk_persuade_tried
set krezk_reason = "persuaded"
Krezk Watchman: ...Huh.
Narrator: He looks at you for a long moment, then turns and bangs the butt of his spear on the gate, three times, slowly.
-> dmitri_comes

~ persuade_fail
set krezk_persuade_tried
Krezk Watchman: Everyone who's ever said that to me wanted to be the door. No.
-> reasons

~ cow_ok
set krezk_reason = "cowed"
Narrator: His knuckles whiten on the spear. Behind the gate, someone shouts a question; he shouts back an answer you don't catch, and it isn't brave.
Krezk Watchman [afraid]: All right. All right! I'm fetching the burgomaster. Stand back from the wall and keep your hands where my friends can see them.
approve godrick_pendlebrook -1 kip_smudgewick -1: You threatened your way through Krezk's gate
-> dmitri_comes

~ cow_fail
set krezk_threatened
Narrator: An arrow thumps into the road a hand's breadth from your boots. Up on the wall-walk, somebody you hadn't noticed is already nocking another.
Krezk Watchman: The wall's very good. Thank you for asking. And now nobody up there will believe a sweet word out of you, so don't waste one.
-> reasons

~ ireena
Krezk Watchman: Kolyan's girl? Wait here. Don't move. I mean that in the friendliest way.
Narrator: He hammers on the gate and calls a name. After a while the wicket opens and a broad, grey-bearded man in a sheepskin steps out, the way a man steps out into hail.
Dmitri Krezkov: Ireena Kolyana. I knew your father. I am Dmitri Krezkov, and Krezk is mine to keep.
Dmitri Krezkov: The devil wants you. Every soul in the valley knows it. You ask me to open my gate and let his want in after you.
interject guest:ireena: I'm not asking you to fight him. I'm asking for a roof he hasn't been under.
if guest:ismark
interject guest:ismark: And if it helps, I'm her brother, and I'll be doing all the fighting anyway.
endif
Narrator: Dmitri looks at Ireena for a long while. Something in his face gives way, slowly, like ice on a thawing pond.
Dmitri Krezkov: Your father sent us salt, the winter the passes closed and we had none. Krezk doesn't forget salt. Open it.
set krezk_reason = "ireena"
set krezk_refuge_offered
-> opened

~ abbot
Krezk Watchman: The Abbot. Of course it's the Abbot. Wait.
Narrator: He bangs on the gate. The man who comes out through the wicket is broad and grey-bearded, wrapped in a sheepskin, with the face of someone who has buried more than he has planted.
Dmitri Krezkov: I'm Dmitri Krezkov, burgomaster. You've been up the mountain. And he sent you down to me with his blessing.
Dmitri Krezkov: If he says you're harmless, you're harmless or you're his. Either way, he'd find another road for you. Open it.
set krezk_reason = "abbot"
-> opened

~ wine
Krezk Watchman: The wine? Wait there. Don't go anywhere. Don't let the wine go anywhere.
Narrator: Shouting behind the gate, and running. A broad, grey-bearded man in a sheepskin comes out through the wicket faster than his dignity would like.
Dmitri Krezkov: Dmitri Krezkov, burgomaster. The Martikovs' wine has come up this road every autumn since my grandfather's time. This year: nothing. No cart, no word.
Dmitri Krezkov: A village that can't drink can still pray, but it does it with less conviction. Come in. Drink our water. Tell me what you know.
set krezk_reason = "wine"
-> opened

~ wolves
Krezk Watchman: I saw. Half the wall saw. Wait.
Narrator: He bangs on the gate. A broad, grey-bearded man in a sheepskin steps out through the wicket and looks at the bodies in the road before he looks at you.
Dmitri Krezkov: Dmitri Krezkov, burgomaster. You bled on our doorstep for us. That's a reason. Open it.
set krezk_reason = "wolves"
-> opened

~ cleric
Krezk Watchman: ...Wait there.
Narrator: He hammers on the gate and calls a name. The broad, grey-bearded man who comes out through the wicket has been crying recently and has made very sure it doesn't show.
Dmitri Krezkov: Dmitri Krezkov, burgomaster. You're a priest. A real one, with a god that answers?
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: He answers. Here, more quietly than I'm used to. But He answers.
if not name:liriel_dawnsong
interject class:cleric: Most days. Not always when I'd like.
endif
Dmitri Krezkov: That's more than mine does. My son is sick. My last son. If your god answers you in my house, you can have anything Krezk owns. Open it.
inspire class:cleric: offered a frightened town a priest at its gate
set krezk_reason = "cleric"
set ilya_heard
quest the_burgomasters_son heard
-> opened

~ dmitri_comes
Narrator: The wicket opens. A broad, grey-bearded man in a sheepskin steps out and looks you over the way a farmer looks at weather.
Dmitri Krezkov: Dmitri Krezkov. Burgomaster. My watchman tells me you're very persuasive.
if flag.krezk_reason == "cowed"
Dmitri Krezkov [angry]: Or very loud. Come in, then. You'd climb it otherwise, and I'd lose men stopping you. Don't make me sorry I counted.
else
Dmitri Krezkov: Nobody has talked their way past that gate in eleven years. I'll let you in to see what that kind of tongue looks like. Open it.
endif
-> opened

~ opened
set krezk_gate_open
quest the_gate_of_krezk opened
if flag.krezk_threatened
Dmitri Krezkov [angry]: And you're the ones who offered to test my wall. My bowman remembers your faces. So will I. Behave inside it.
endif
if flag.vallaki_backed == "wachter"
Dmitri Krezkov: One thing. Word came up from Vallaki that Fiona Wachter sits in the burgomaster's chair now, and that strangers put her there. If that was you, keep it to yourselves inside my wall.
elif flag.vallaki_backed == "neither"
Dmitri Krezkov: Word came from Vallaki that the town threw out its Baron and put a priest and an innkeeper in charge. If you had a hand in it, I'd shake it. Once.
endif
Narrator: The bar comes up with a groan. The gate opens a body's width, no more, and waits for you to fit yourselves through it.
Dmitri Krezkov: Inside. Quickly. We don't hold it open for weather. My house is the big one past the well, if you've business with Krezk.
set dmitri_met
-> END

~ guard
if flag.abbot_fate == "repentant"
Krezk Watchman: Saw a light go up the mountain at dawn. Not a lamp. Walked off the top of the peak, the Belviews say, and kept going. The burgomaster went up to the shrine and sat there an hour.
elif flag.abbot_fate == "slain"
Krezk Watchman: The abbey's quiet. First time in my life I've looked up at it and not felt looked back at. I don't know if I like it.
elif flag.abbot_fate == "wedding"
Krezk Watchman: A cart went down the road last night, with something in a white dress sitting up very straight in the back. Nobody here waved.
elif flag.abbot_fate == "broken"
Krezk Watchman: The Belviews come down for bread now. They say the Abbot doesn't. Doesn't eat, doesn't speak, just sits. They seem to think that's our fault. Maybe it is.
elif night
Krezk Watchman: Gate's barred for the night. If you're inside, stay inside. If you're out here with me, keep talking. It helps.
else
Krezk Watchman: Still in one piece? Good. Krezk likes visitors who stay that way. Fewer graves.
endif
* Heard anything interesting? -> news
* Tell us about the Abbey. -> about_abbey
* Goodbye. -> END

~ news
if flag.abbot_told_strahd
Krezk Watchman: Bats. A cloud of them came down off the abbey at dusk and went east, toward the castle, like they were carrying a letter. The burgomaster's had the gate doubled.
endif
if flag.wards_cells_freed
Krezk Watchman: There's Belviews on the mountainside. Not the usual ones; worse ones, thin and wild, digging in the snow for roots. The Abbot's let them out, or someone has.
endif
if flag.ilya_fate == "healed"
Krezk Watchman: The burgomaster's boy is up and about. Running, even. First thing he did was try to climb the wall. We let him. Nobody's had the heart to tell him off.
elif flag.ilya_fate == "frail"
Krezk Watchman: The burgomaster's boy is out of bed. Pale as milk, but out of bed. Anna carries him to the well and back every morning so he can see the sky.
elif flag.ilya_heard
Krezk Watchman: The burgomaster's boy is no better. People go quiet passing that house. You can hear Anna singing through the shutters, and you can hear her stop.
else
set ilya_heard
quest the_burgomasters_son heard
Krezk Watchman: The burgomaster's boy is sick. A fever since the spring. His last son, Dmitri says. You can hear Anna singing to him through the shutters every night, and you can hear her stop.
endif
if not flag.wizard_of_wines_hook and not flag.wine_shortage_heard
Krezk Watchman: And the wine's stopped. The Martikovs' cart came every autumn. Not this one.
if not quest.wizard_of_wines
quest wizard_of_wines rumored
endif
endif
if not flag.werewolf_rumor and not flag.den_children_freed
set werewolf_rumor
if not quest.wolves_in_the_hills
quest wolves_in_the_hills heard
endif
Krezk Watchman: Five children gone from the farms below the wall this year. Wolves, they say. Wolves don't lift latches. There's a den up in the hills over the lake, the shepherds say, and the shepherds don't go up there any more.
endif
if not quest.lighter_than_it_should_be
set krezk_toys_rumor
quest lighter_than_it_should_be rumored
Krezk Watchman: And there are toys on the Krezkov graves at the pool every morning. Carved ones: horses, wolves. Nobody in Krezk carves like that. Dmitri smashes them. Anna keeps them.
elif flag.sorin_fate == "home"
Krezk Watchman: The burgomaster's got a son home who went up the mountain twenty years ago. I don't understand it and I'm not asking. Anna's singing again. All day.
endif
-> END

~ about_abbey
Krezk Watchman: Up there? Holy house, once. My grandmother went up to the nuns when her chest was bad and came back singing. Nobody goes up singing now.
Krezk Watchman: The Abbot came after the nuns were gone. Looks younger than me. Looked younger than my grandmother, too, when she was alive. Folk go up sick and come down well, or they don't come down.
if flag.abbot_met
interject tag:curious: Who doesn't come down?
Krezk Watchman: Ask him about the Belviews. Or don't. I'd rather you didn't, in the end; you might get an answer.
endif
-> END
